Since April, people have told us their bookings land on the wrong day. By 4 October the desk had
merged 412 reports here, on subject line alone.

**Split into three problems.** Reading the bodies showed that #4471 held three bugs, not one.
[The split](/kb/incidents/4471/split) counts each one and says how they differ.

- **parser**: the parser reads dates month first, and our tenants write the day first. This stays
  in #4471. The fix is queued.
- **hint**: booking-v3 prints a month-first date hint. Its reports moved to
  [#2](https://github.com/0uykjh/kb-4471-split/issues/2).
- **clock**: the booking keeps its date and moves one day. Its reports moved to
  [#3](https://github.com/0uykjh/kb-4471-split/issues/3).

<Callout>
Split. #4471 is the parser bug only; the other two problems have their own tickets.
</Callout>

